# *** DO NOT RUN THIS FILE AS IT STANDS - IT USES A KEYWORD ORCA DOES NOT HAVE ***
# ORCA has no "Counterpoise" keyword, and a %geom Fragments block is not the
# supported way to define the fragments. The working counterpoise inputs are
#   ../../03_tier2_completion/jobs/scope2/*.inp
# and they use the construction from the ORCA 6.1.1 manual (section 2.11.1):
#   %frag
#     Definition
#       1 {0 1 2 ... 21} end
#       2 {22 ... 29} end
#     end
#   end
#   %geom
#     GhostFrags {1} end      # the other job uses {2}
#   end
# This file is kept only as a record of what was planned before the audit.

# TIER 3 - counterpoise-corrected adsorption energy, single point (cloud instance)
# Fragment 1 = framework cluster (atoms 0:21), fragment 2 = adsorbate.
# For V-PRC: adsorbate atoms 22:29 (H3VO4). For W-PRC: atoms 22:24 (H2O).
# ORCA atom numbering inside blocks is ZERO-based.

! PBE0 D3BJ def2-TZVP RIJCOSX TightSCF DefGrid3 Counterpoise

%geom
  Fragments
    1 {0:21} end
    2 {22:29} end
  end
end

%pal nprocs 12 end
%maxcore 4000

* xyzfile 0 1 t2_prc.xyz
